    "name": "AI Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships",
    "slug": "ai-sales-marketing-and-partnerships",
    "count": 54,
    "guide": "Jobs in this category center on getting AI products in front of buyers and building the partnerships that make that possible. Day to day work includes running account executive pipelines for AI platforms, writing go to market strategy for new AI features, managing partner and channel relationships, and building product marketing that explains what an AI system does to non technical buyers. This differs from Applied AI, where the work is building or tuning models and integrating them into a product, and from Solutions Engineering, where the work is technical pre sales support answering how a product fits a customer's stack. People in Sales, Marketing, and Partnerships are measured on revenue, partner agreements, and market awareness rather than model performance or implementation details, even though they need enough technical fluency to speak credibly about the product.\n\nA bachelor's degree shows up across postings but rarely reads as a hard requirement here. Degree fields range from business or communications for marketing and account roles to technical undergraduate degrees for business development titles tied to infrastructure and physical AI companies like CoreWeave, Nebius, and Lightning AI. Our sample did not surface any specific AI sales or marketing certification named consistently by employers, so a claimed \"AI sales certificate\" should not be treated as a real hiring signal based on this data. What actually shows up more often is a demonstrated sales or marketing track record combined with comfort discussing AI products in front of technical buyers.\n\nSeniority in our sample skews toward experienced hires. Titles cluster around Manager, Director, Senior, and Staff levels at companies such as Anthropic, Cloudflare, Databricks, and UiPath, with a smaller number of Principal and Executive titles mixed in. Entry points do exist, mostly labeled Intern, Junior, or Working Student, including a Cloudflare AI Innovation Intern in service sales and a Junior AI Go to Market Engineer role at FTAPI. The common path into a mid or senior role here is prior sales, marketing, or partnerships experience in software, then a move into an AI focused company, rather than starting an AI career directly in sales.\n\nWhere postings do list technical skills, the most common are cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, and Azure, plus familiarity with large language models, model evaluation, prompt engineering, and fine tuning concepts. Databricks appears both as an employer name and as a named platform skill, and Okta shows up the same way on identity focused listings. Some go to market engineering and business development postings also name Python or SQL, reflecting roles that blend sales work with light scripting or data tasks. Many of the marketing and account executive postings in our sample list no structured skills at all, which suggests the real qualifying signal for those roles sits in the written job description and required experience rather than a tools checklist.\n\nWe currently track approximately 47 open postings in this category as of today. Only 2 of the 106 postings we pulled carried an actual salary figure, a Machine Learning Sales Engineer role at Lightning AI listed at $187,409 per year and a Machine Learning Engineer, Growth role at Whatnot listed at $281,892 per year, so any salary reference here reflects a two posting sample and not a market rate. The companies posting most often in this category are UiPath, Anthropic, Cloudflare, Databricks, ServiceNow, and Nebius, spanning agentic automation, foundation model, cloud infrastructure, and enterprise software vendors. A large share of the remaining postings come from smaller European employers listed through general job boards, often for go to market engineering or business development roles that pair AI product knowledge with traditional sales and marketing duties. Given how thin the salary data is, job seekers should treat any compensation figures here as directional and confirm real numbers directly with employers.",
